<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>Article 6 Tax Deferral Treatment for Transfer
and Foreign Exchange Registration</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>6.1 Tax Treatment.</B> The Parties confirm
that this transaction is an asset transfer in which the consideration is paid in the form of stock of an overseas listed company (YMT).
The Sellers shall use their best efforts to apply for the special tax treatment (tax deferral) under the tax laws and regulations of the
People&rsquo;s Republic of China; however, the Parties expressly acknowledge that there is no guarantee that the competent tax authority
will recognize this transaction as qualifying for the special tax treatment. If the application is not accepted or recognized, or the
deferral is recovered, and the actual income tax, late payment surcharge, interest and reasonable defense expenses paid by the Sellers
in connection with this transaction exceed the amount payable under the &ldquo;<B>Five-Year Deferral Assumption</B>&rdquo;, the excess
shall be fully compensated by the Buyer in cash within thirty (30) days after the Sellers actually pay the tax.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>6.2 Deferral Tax Filing.</B> After the expiration
of the Asset and Business Rectification Period and the completion of the transaction, the Sellers shall apply to the competent tax authority
for the special-tax-treatment deferral filing and submit the relevant materials. The Buyer shall cooperate in providing all documents
and information required for the deferral filing, including without limitation this Agreement and share issuance certificates.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>6.3 Treatment of Transfers During Deferral
Period.</B> Within the Five-Year Deferral Period, if the Sellers transfer all or part of the consideration shares (including those converted
into ADSs), the Sellers shall calculate and pay the corresponding income tax on the transferred portion. The un-transferred portion shall
continue to enjoy tax deferral treatment until the end of the deferral period or until all remaining shares are transferred (whichever
occurs first). If, at the expiration of the deferral period, the remaining shares have not yet been fully transferred, the Sellers may
continue to defer the income tax corresponding to such remaining shares until the actual transfer date; the Buyer shall not claim any
rights against the Sellers or require the Sellers to bear additional costs as a result of the expiration of the deferral period.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>6.4 Foreign Exchange Registration.</B> Since
the consideration for this transaction is paid in the form of stock of an overseas listed company (YMT), the Sellers, as domestic entities,
shall complete the foreign exchange registration for offshore direct investment or offshore securities investment with the State Administration
of Foreign Exchange or its authorized branches after the Asset and Business Rectification Period ends and the transaction is completed.
The Buyer shall, within fifteen (15) business days after the expiration of the Asset and Business Rectification Period and the completion
of the transaction, provide the Sellers with all Cayman company documents required for foreign exchange registration (including without
limitation YMT&rsquo;s articles of association, register of members, share certificate, certificate of registered agent, etc.) and shall
cooperate with the Sellers in completing such registration.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>6.5 Trading After Foreign Exchange Registration.</B>
The Sellers shall only be entitled to convert the unlocked consideration shares into ADSs and trade them on the Nasdaq market after completing
the foreign exchange registration procedures. If the Sellers fail to complete the foreign exchange registration due to reasons attributable
to the Buyer (including but not limited to the Buyer&rsquo;s failure to provide the required documents for registration in a timely manner,
the inability of YMT&rsquo;s stock to be normally traded on Nasdaq, etc.), the Buyer shall be deemed to have improperly failed to deliver
the consideration shares, and the Sellers shall have the right to elect: (a) to require the Buyer to bear liability for breach under Article
11.1; or (b) to suspend the performance of post-asset-transfer cooperation obligations, without bearing any liability for breach, until
the foreign exchange registration is completed. If the Sellers have completed the foreign exchange registration but, due to reasons attributable
to themselves, transfer shares before completing such registration, the legal risks and administrative liability arising therefrom shall
be borne by the Sellers themselves.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>Article 7 Closing and Post-Closing Obligations</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

